      "full_original_title_TeX": "Rational-point undecidability for smooth projective varieties over the rational numbers",
      "full_original_abstract_TeX": "\nCombining OpenAI's negative solution of rational Hilbert's tenth problem\nwith Poonen's established effective transfer, we obtain undecidability of\nrational-point existence for arbitrary smooth projective geometrically\nintegral varieties over $\\Q$. We specify a homogeneous-equation input\npromise and reconstruct the terminating contradiction algorithm. There is\nalso no computable uniform bound on the height of one rational point in\nterms of the size of the presented equations. The arithmetic input is used\nwith two explicit corrections documented here and in the accompanying\nverification supplement. This is a geometric consequence of that input;\nneither the geometric reduction nor the base undecidability theorem is\nclaimed as a new independent solution.\n",
